      trivia: "Mombacho laboured under the unusual handicap of being unable to trade under its own name in the United States. The “Mombacho” trademark had been applied for in 2003 and registered in 2004 by Tropical Tobacco (Tabacalera Tropical — the company behind Casa Fernández, known today as AGANORSA Leaf); Mombacho sought its cancellation in 2016 but was rebuffed by the USPTO. The brand therefore had no choice but to sell in the American market as “Tierra Volcán” (volcanic earth), and after the 2021 lawsuit and settlement it was renamed “Favilli” from December 2021. In the end the brand finished its life never once able to bear its own name in the United States. Its home, Casa Favilli — built in 1925 and held to be Granada’s first reinforced-concrete building, a designated historic monument — was at once a factory and a tourist landmark, but in its final years it lost its manufacturing role, was converted into an experiential centre, and was put up for sale when the business closed. The brand that began with a vow on a volcano’s summit quietly lowered its curtain in June 2023, after seventeen years of history."
