        "Gurkha Nicaragua Series Toro — 6 × 54. Unveiled at the 2019 IPCPR, shipped that October. Wrapper, double binder and filler all AGANORSA-grown Corojo 99/Criollo 98; made at TABSA in Estelí. The line also includes a Robusto 5 × 52, Belicoso 6⅛ × 52, Magnum 6 × 60 and a TAA-exclusive figurado 6⅞ × 52",
        "Gurkha Treinta Toro — 2019, marking the brand’s 30th anniversary (treinta = thirty). Ecuadorian Habano rosado wrapper / AGANORSA Corojo 99 binder / Corojo 99 and Criollo 98 fillers from Estelí and Jalapa. Made at TABSA",
        "Gurkha Cellar Reserve 15 Year Hedonism — 6 × 58. A line claiming 15-year-aged leaf; Criollo 98 wrapper over a Dominican Olor binder. The line also includes the Solara 5 × 58",
        "Gurkha Cellar Reserve Platinum — Ecuadorian oscuro wrapper with binder and filler from Condega, Estelí and Jalapa aged up to twelve years. Made by American Caribbean Tobacco S.A. in Estelí",
        "Gurkha Ghost Asura — 6 × 54. Brazilian Arapiraca wrapper / Dominican Criollo 98 binder / Dominican and Nicaraguan fillers. Made in the Dominican Republic (the line’s Connecticut version, the Shadow, is 5 × 52)",
        "Gurkha Ghost Zombie Mini — 4 × 34 petit corona. Introduced in 2026 in tins as the smallest size of the Ghost family",
